id: pm-2i12ti
title: "GH-709: batch duplicate-cluster sweep with canonical precomputed similarity signals"
description: "Add a public SDK batch duplicate sweep that reads a tracker once, precomputes canonical title tokens and issue-code signals, collapses unordered pairs into deterministic clusters, and gives multi-agent branch merges a practical post-merge duplicate detector without reimplementing CLI scoring."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[7]: "area:multi-agent","area:performance","area:sdk",context-management,duplicates,gh-issue,"gh:unbraind/pm-cli#709"
created_at: "2026-07-25T12:55:49.904Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-25T15:27:31.506Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-25T15:27:30.546Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "The public SDK exposes a bounded batch duplicate sweep that reads tracker metadata once and preserves exact-title, issue-code, and token-overlap scoring parity; Results collapse unordered pairs deterministically and support threshold, status, since, and result bounds suitable for large trackers; A benchmark regression proves a full sweep does not perform one tracker scan per candidate or re-tokenize every title per pair; CLI, SDK docs, contracts, and 100 percent coverage remain aligned"
parent: pm-usfg
resolution: The SDK provides a bounded one-read duplicate-cluster sweep with prepared signals and disclosed cost.
expected_result: The SDK provides a bounded one-read duplicate-cluster sweep with prepared signals and disclosed cost.
actual_result: "The SDK provides a bounded one-read duplicate-cluster sweep with prepared signals and disclosed cost. Verification: linked tests, full coverage, static/security gates, and packed consumer passed."
