comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T12:55:49.904Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: all-status searches covered the closed create-time advisory pm-4ri6, SDK-first epic pm-usfg, graph duplicate governance, search similarity, and closed indexed-read/performance work. None owns the post-merge batch sweep, precomputed canonical issue-code signal, or deterministic duplicate clusters requested by GH-709; this item is the canonical residual owner."
  "2026-07-25T15:25:48.047Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: tracker-owned test-all completed 13 items / 13 links with 10 unique commands passed, 3 duplicate commands safely skipped, and zero failures, timeouts, empty runs, or sandbox collisions. Final broad suite passed 6,367 tests with 100% statements/branches/functions/lines (43,881/31,106/8,950/42,627). ESLint, zero-clone jscpd, 100% module/export/member docstrings, package boundary, token budgets, SDK surface snapshot, typecheck, contracts, secret scan, pnpm audit (zero vulnerabilities), SDK import costs, and the unchanged CLI transport floor passed. Exact packed tarball consumer proof installed all 15 first-party packages, strict extension doctor returned zero warnings/failures, SDK import succeeded, and Plan create/close/delete/tombstone lifecycle was verified in an isolated temporary project. Tracker health and history drift are clean; graph coverage reports zero active isolates and zero degree<=1 active nodes."
  "2026-07-25T15:26:01.415Z","harness:codex","Implementation: public SDK batch duplicate clustering reads metadata once, prepares normalization/tokens/issue codes once per item, indexes candidate signals, caps work at 1,000,000 pairs, returns deterministic connected components and explicit cost."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T15:26:17.721Z","harness:codex",Whole-tracker similarity should invert deterministic signals into bounded candidate pairs and reuse prepared text; repeated per-item tracker scans are both slower and less transparent than one disclosed batch cost.
